## Local workflow

```bash
mise trust
mise install
mise run check
{% if stack == 'python' or stack == 'typescript' or stack == 'dotnet' -%}
mise run test
{% endif -%}
```

`mise run check` runs `pre-commit run --all-files`, the same hook configuration CI uses. It installs the toolchains declared in `mise.toml` first.

{% if stack == 'python' -%}
`mise run test` runs pytest and writes `coverage/coverage.xml`.
{% elif stack == 'typescript' -%}
`mise run test` runs Vitest with coverage and writes `coverage/coverage-final.json` and `coverage/lcov.info`.
{% elif stack == 'dotnet' -%}
`mise run test` runs `dotnet test` and writes Cobertura coverage under `coverage/`.
{% elif stack == 'unity' -%}
Unity integrity checks do not need the editor:

```bash
uvx --from git+https://github.com/{{ owner }}/dev-platform@{{ platform_ref }}#subdirectory=cli devctl unity integrity
```

Full Unity verification runs on the repository's self-hosted runner.
{% endif %}

## Continuous integration

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` calls the shared platform workflows at `{{ platform_ref }}`. It also runs on pull requests, so the required checks are the same for humans and automation.

{% if stack == 'unity' -%}
Required checks are `platform-verify / integrity`, `platform-verify / tests` and `platform-security / scan`. Unity tests run only on a runner labeled `[self-hosted, windows, unity]`.
{% else -%}
Required checks are `platform-verify / check`, {% if stack != 'other' %}`platform-verify / test` and {% endif %}`platform-security / scan`.
{% endif %}

## Dependency updates

Renovate reads `renovate.json` and extends the shared preset `github>{{ owner }}/dev-platform`. It pins GitHub Actions to commit digests, groups template updates and automerges minor, patch and digest updates after the required checks pass.

## Releases

{% if stack == 'other' -%}
Releases are not configured for this stack-agnostic profile.
{% else -%}
Conventional commits drive release-please. Merging a Release PR creates the tag; `.github/workflows/release.yml` builds the artifact and attaches it to the release.
{% endif %}

## Template updates

The Copier answers file records the template version. Update the platform layer with:

```bash
uvx copier update --defaults
```

Review the resulting diff before committing. Application source, dependencies and the README are project-owned and are not overwritten by template updates.
